  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2022_W22_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-22",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2022_W22_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-22.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2022-06-03",
  "report_week": "22",
  "report_period": "Week 22 (27th May to 3rd Jun 2022)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Ever Stella Shipping have sold their Capesize \"Stella Flora\" 176/2012 Shanghai Jiangnan, China (SS/DD 10/2022, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers Safe Bulkers for USD 31,75 mill basis SS/DD passed. Remind you that same buyers acquired the \"Stella Anita\" 180/2012 Dalian, China (SS 01/2027, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) back in April at USD 30 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Majulah Harbourfront\" 82/2014 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 11/2024, DD 10/2022, BWTS fitted) from Kambara Kisen was sold to Greek buyers for USD 31,6 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Capricorn Moon\" 81/2015 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 04/2025, DD 04/2023, BWTS fitted) of Meiji Shipping was sold to German buyers for region USD 34 mill. On the Ultramax sector, Cido Shipping's \"Fortune Bell\" 61/2020 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 05/2025, DD 05/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 39 mill, while the three-years-older sister vessel \"Pavo Bright\" 61/2017 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 01/2027, DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold to Greek buyers for mid-high USD 33 mill. The Supramax \"Bao Chuan\" 56/2007 Mitsui, Japan (SS 04/2027, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold to Chinese buyers for USD 17,8 mill. Note that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Therese Selmer\" 55/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS 09/2026, DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at USD 17,5 mill basis delivery July-August 2022. Moreover, the \"Evnia\" 53/2003 New Century, China (SS/DD 08/2023) was sold for USD 14,4 mill, while same owners sold the sister vessel \"Nicolaos A.\" 53/2003 New Century, China (SS/DD 03/2023) in May at the same price. Stam Shipping have sold two Handysize vessels, the \"Cetus Star\" 33/2004 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 10/2024) to Chinese buyers for high USD 12 mill and the OHBS \"Cassiopeia Star\" 32/2005 Naikai, Japan (SS/DD 03/2025, DD 03/2023) to Turkish buyers for USD 13,3 mill. In addition, the OHBS \"Conception Light\" 32/2007 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 12/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold to undisclosed buyers at USD 15,7 mill.",
    "tankers": "RB Armatori have committed their Aframax \"Rumford\" 107/2012 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers Thenamaris for USD 32,7 mill. Moreover, the \"Mitera Marigo\" 105/2007 Sumitomo, Japan (SS 01/2027, DD 08/2024) of Atlas Maritime was sold to Singaporean buyers for USD 24,95 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Banda Sea\" 105/2007 Sumitomo, Japan (SS/DD 05/2022, Scrubber fitted) was sold back in April at USD 21 mill. The MR2 \"Pacific Diamond\" 48/2010 Iwagi, Japan (SS 10/2025, DD 12/2023, BWTS fitted) from Eastern Pacific Shipping was sold for USD 18 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"Jal Sasvata\" 46/2009 Naikai, Japan (SS 04/2024, DD 08/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 17 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 13,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 20,000/22,000 pd range. Trips from China into Indonesia were fixed around usd 29,000/30,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into Philippines were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into Persian Gulf were fixed around usd 27,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via North Coast South America were fixed around usd 23,000/25,000 pd. Continental trips via North Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 31,000/33,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into China were fixed around usd 28,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 800K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed around usd 27,000/28,000 pd. Trips from Philippines into China with nickel ore were reported at the level of usd 28,000 pd. Continental trips into South Africa were fixed around usd 25,000/26,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Red Sea into East Africa were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent were fixed around usd 35,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 28,000/30,000 pd. An Ultramax was reported fixed at the level of usd 39,500 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery India with redelivery Persian Gulf/Japan range.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "No fixture reported for this segment. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
